                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238729607",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197960410281",
                            "num_reviews": 9,
                            "playtime_forever": 310,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 310,
                            "last_played": 1419218109
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Boycotting these guys. One of the first early access games I backed and it left me with a bitter taste in my mouth.\n\nLosing everything due to server issues is 100% a lie. No devs in this day and age do without version control. Cloud bucket storage is also hilariously cheap for anything required for this tier of game, like I'm talking if all code and assets were ONE TERABYTE, they'd be paying something like $23 per month for storage. So if you believe what they say about having lost everything you're letting them insult your intelligence. I understand if they're deciding to move on because this was a concept game and they are moving on to other projects, but to not be able to own that and choosing instead lie to their customers is unforgivable, as if we don't have enough lack of accountability in this world already.\n\nEdit: I'm not saying they don't deserve a second chance because everyone makes mistakes, but there's a right way and a wrong way to do things and by choosing to shove things under the rug they definitely picked the latter.",
